## MINI-GAME 5: CLEAN THE SOLAR PANELS

This mini-game represents one of the most important repair operations on Mars.

The player must clean the dust-covered solar panels to restore power to the damaged machines.

### Main objective

Remove the thick red dust covering the solar panels.

### Visual design

The screen should show a large pixel-art solar panel.

The panel contains several rectangular solar cells.

Each cell is covered with red Martian dust.

A small cleaning tool appears beside the panel.

The player must move the tool across the dirty surface.

### Controls

- Mouse click and drag to clean.
- Touch and drag on mobile.
- Optional keyboard cleaning mode.

### Gameplay mechanics

The player moves the cleaning tool across the panel.

Dust disappears gradually wherever the tool passes.

The panel's energy meter increases as more surface area is cleaned.

The player must clean a required percentage of the panel before the timer expires.

### Objective

Clean at least 90% of the solar panel.

### Challenges

- Dust may move back onto some areas.
- Some solar cells require extra cleaning.
- The player should avoid damaging the panel surface.
- The timer adds urgency.

### Feedback

When a cell becomes clean, it should glow slightly.

The energy meter should rise.

