## MEETING SPIRIT

Spirit introduces herself.

She explains that she was one of NASA's Mars Exploration Rover twin missions.

She landed in Gusev Crater on January 4, 2004.

Her original mission was planned to last approximately 90 Martian days.

However, she continued working for more than six years.

Her main objective was to investigate Martian rocks and soil and search for evidence of past water.

She proudly remembers exploring hills and rocky terrain.

She traveled approximately 7.7 kilometers across Mars.

Then she tells Jack about the difficult final part of her mission.

In 2009, her wheels became trapped in soft Martian soil.

NASA tried to free her.

However, she could not escape.

Her last confirmed communication with Earth was received on March 22, 2010.

The group listens quietly.

